        <!-- Section 5: Strategic Insights -->
        <section id="exam-prep-insights">
            <h2>5. Strategic Insights for Exam Preparation</h2>

            <h3>For Educators & Curriculum Planners</h3>

            <h4>Priority 1: High-Frequency, Always-Tested Topics</h4>
            <p>These topics appear in 80–100% of examination years and should receive the most instructional time:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Database Fundamentals</strong> — Primary/Foreign keys, DBMS vs RDBMS, relational models, table/form/report objects in MS-Access, SQL basics (DML/DDL), entity relationships</li>
                <li><strong>C Programming: Loops</strong> — for, while, do-while syntax; nested loops; difference between loop types; continue/break statements</li>
                <li><strong>C Programming: Operators</strong> — Arithmetic, relational, logical, assignment; operator precedence; increment/decrement (++, --)</li>
                <li><strong>C Programming: Functions</strong> — Function declaration, prototype, void, return statement, user-defined vs library functions</li>
                <li><strong>Control Structures</strong> — if-else, switch-case, else-if ladder; decision-making syntax</li>
            </ul>

            <h4>Priority 2: Moderate-Frequency Topics</h4>
            <p>These topics appear in 50–79% of years and deserve regular coverage:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Data Types & Format Specifiers</strong> — %d, %f, %c, %s, %lf, %ld; int, float, char, double sizes</li>
                <li><strong>Variables & Constants</strong> — Declaration, initialization, local vs global scope</li>
                <li><strong>Input/Output Functions</strong> — printf, scanf, gets, getch, putchar, getc</li>
                <li><strong>Escape Sequences</strong> — \n, \t, \\</li>
                <li><strong>Preprocessor Directives</strong> — #include, #define</li>
                <li><strong>Keywords/Reserved Words</strong> — case, break, continue, return, void</li>
            </ul>

            <h4>Priority 3: Emerging or Under-Tested Topics</h4>
            <p>Based on recent trends (2024–2025), these topics show increasing frequency:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Bitwise Operators</strong> — &, |, ^, ~ (appeared prominently in 2025)</li>
                <li><strong>Storage Classes</strong> — auto, static, extern, register (2025 Long question)</li>
                <li><strong>Binary Search / Algorithm Complexity</strong> (2025 Long question)</li>
                <li><strong>Normalization</strong> (appeared in 2022, 2024 Long questions)</li>
                <li><strong>ACID Properties</strong> (appeared in 2025)</li>
            </ul>

